# Corpus unit rebench-nanogpt_chat_rl/C04 — gap (mandatory-CQ-unmet path; batch: rebench)
#
# Source: rebench-nanogpt_chat_rl C04 annotation (implementation-behavioral,
# analytic_proof; corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: pairwise single-elimination tournament
# selection is judge-call-optimal for best-of-N — at N=8 it uses N-1 = 7 judge calls per prompt
# vs 28 for round-robin, with ceil(log2 N) = 3 dependent latency rounds under parallel dispatch.
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * scheme = analytic_proof (annotated strict) -> corpus-v1 `analytic_argument(P, Prf)`
#     (defeasible). Per LOWERING, the 6 strict-flavored annotations still lower through
#     analytic_argument; the arithmetic/table-recheck strict adapter does not exist yet
#     (migration to a strict rule + certificate is future work). Counting identities (7, 28, 3)
#     stay in nl and refs; the formal atom is the instantiated conclusion
#     holds_analytically(tournament_judge_call_optimal).
#   * BOTH mandatory CQs are unmet-gap:
#       - assumptions_hold (assumptions_established): annotation CQ2 — the N-1 lower bound presumes
#         a consistent comparator, but the Llama-3-8b judge randomizes pair order and returns
#         nondeterministic verdicts (N100 approach_context, N104: bit-identical weights scored
#         differently), so the deterministic optimality argument's key assumption fails.
#       - scope_licensed (scope_licensed): annotation CQ1 — no experiment inspects the tournament
#         code path; E03, the only cited experiment, verifies C03 and covers generation-parameter
#         alignment, so the code citation in C04's Proof stands in for an inspection nobody ran.
#     The incomplete analytic_argument(...) is declared as a located hole with
#     `open assumptions_hold` and `open scope_licensed` (lowering re-done for issue #15 under
#     `lara-core@0.3`); `gap` on empty complete support.
#   * Dead end N604 is annotated `decision: undercut` of the latency sub-claim's support (a
#     tournament run stalled under a 429 judge storm, so within-round parallelism did not deliver
#     round-bounded latency). Per LOWERING Attacks, with a mandatory CQ independently unmet the gap
#     rule wins. The undercut is now declared against the hole's root (leaf u1 concluding the
#     analytic_argument exception unsound_assumption, challenge d1, `undercut d1 a1.rule`): it
#     type-checks and is inert, because no complete argument contains a1's root. The annotator
#     flagged N604 as a coin-flip undercut-vs-none; it changes no status either way.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact rebench-nanogpt_chat_rl at sha256:170bca122d75
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------

claim c04
  nl      = "Pairwise single-elimination tournament selection is judge-call-optimal for best-of-N: at N=8 it uses N-1 = 7 judge calls per prompt vs 28 for round-robin, with ceil(log2 N) = 3 dependent latency rounds under parallel dispatch"
  formal  = holds_analytically(tournament_judge_call_optimal)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- The derivation premise is present ... ------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: the counting derivation (single-elim on 8 uses 4+2+1 = 7 = N-1 calls;
# round-robin 28; depth ceil(log2 8) = 3), from the shipped tournament loop.
leaf e1 : derives(tournament_counting_derivation, tournament_judge_call_optimal)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C04, rl_finetune_best_of_n.py#118-139, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N05]

# Dead end N604: a tournament run on the same judge stalled under a 429 storm, so the derivation's
# parallel-dispatch => round-bounded-latency assumption fails when the shared judge throttles.
leaf u1 : unsound_assumption(tournament_judge_call_optimal)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N604]

# --- ... and the incomplete argument is a located hole ------------------------------------------

# assumptions_established(tournament_counting_derivation) has no honest leaf — the judge is not a
# consistent comparator (N100/N104) — and scope_licensed is unmet — no experiment inspects the
# tournament code path (E03 verifies only C03) — so both mandatory questions stay open.
arg a1 : supports(c04) by analytic_argument(tournament_judge_call_optimal, tournament_counting_derivation)
  open assumptions_hold
  open scope_licensed

# --- N604 undercuts the latency inference (gap rule wins: inert on a hole) ---------------------

# Licensed by `exception analytic_argument : unsound_assumption(P)` (corpus-v1). The target is the
# root of the hole a1, so the attack is kept but produces no edge.
arg d1 : challenges(assumptions_hold(a1)) by leaf(u1)
undercut d1 a1.rule

status c04

